# sede_thirst_cues.voc
#
# WHAT: words that, appearing near "sede", signal the THIRST reading —
#       closed e, /ˈsedɨ/ ("matar a sede", "sede de poder", "morto de sede").
# WHERE USED: bifonia/scoring.py → resolve_sense(), the meaning tiebreaker for
#       "sede" (both senses are NOUNS — POS cannot tell them apart).
# EFFECT: each cue token in the ±3 window adds to the "thirst" score; higher of
#       seat/thirst wins, ties default to thirst (the prototypical reading).
#       Two cue families: (1) physical-thirst collocates — quench/feel/dying-of;
#       (2) abstract desires that follow "sede de X" (figurative thirst).
# HOW TO EXTEND: add quench/feel verbs, body/heat nouns, or abstract-desire nouns
#       that take "sede de …". One term per line, lowercase.
# ── physical thirst: quench / feel / suffer ──
matar
mata
matava
matou
saciar
saciava
sacia
saciou
aplacar
aplacava
ter
tem
tinha
tenho
sentir
sentia
sente
queixou
queixava
morto
mortos
morrer
morria
morrendo
desidratação
garganta
boca
seca
calor
deserto
água
beber
bebida
sequioso
sequiosa
ressente
# ── figurative "sede de X": abstract desires ──
poder
vingança
conhecimento
saber
